// spec: LEX-031
//
// The diagnostic names the line the string OPENED on -- the one place the
// fault certainly is -- not the line the scan reached, which is the end of the
// file.
//
// ⚠️ The filler below carries NO QUOTES, and that is the point.  This case was
// defects/DEF-07, whose filler was 'WriteLn (''filler'');' four times: those
// quotes PAIR UP with the stray one, so the genuinely unterminated string
// opened on the last filler line and the fix moved the answer by one. The case
// claimed the filler existed "so that a fix is visible in the recording rather
// than being a difference of one", and it did the opposite.

var A := 1;
var B := 2;

WriteLn ('oops);

var C := 3;
var D := 4;
var E := 5;
var F := 6;
